From b39d8bdb7bae7186ed93829b67b4fcbd52fd115f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Hardy <matt@deuso.de>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:02:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] impulse: make the audio thread RT-safe (lock-free IR swap, no
 alloc)

- IR handoff is a lock-free raw-pointer atomic exchange: the worker builds
  the convolver and publishes via pendingConv_; the audio thread adopts it,
  never locks
- Replaced convolvers retire through an SPSC ring and are freed on the worker
  (FFT buffer frees off the realtime path)
- Waveform display uses the seqlock pattern; takeIrWaveform retries lock-free
- Rebuild requests use an atomic flag polled by the worker (no condvar signal
  from the audio thread)
- Scratch pre-allocated in setupProcessing to max(maxSamplesPerBlock, 8192)

GPL-3.0-or-later.
